    "methods_description": "Participants completed a main instruction-following task in which four sequential instruction screens (200 ms display, 800 ms interscreen interval) informed attention allocation (integration vs. selection), relevant stimulus category, relevant feature (color or shape), and response mapping, followed by target images (200 ms) framed by colored shapes. Catch trials required a dual keypress response. A separate 1-back localizer task presented one image per trial, requiring participants to judge subcategory repetition via keypress. The main task consisted of 16 blocks of 32 trials each, and the localizer task consisted of 8 blocks of 40 trials, with block order counterbalanced across the session. EEG data were recorded during these tasks and organized using bids-matlab-tools.",
